{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612725-welcome-to-the-world-of-tomorrow","id":612725,"title":"Welcome to the world of tomorrow!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-02T15:42:48-07:00","id":612725,"title":"Welcome to the world of tomorrow!","content":"So one thing that I have difficulty with is the duration of time that can pass in world in a campaign for vampire. In most games years, or decades at most will pass. But for vampire, to get the players to blood potency 3 or 4 without diablere would take some time. This brings up two problems for me.<br /> <br /> First, and probably the most simple, is a lot of time skips. Is it acceptable to say. &quot;Okay, ten years pass. What did your character do to pass the time?&quot;<br /> <br /> Secondly, and more difficult for me, is the changes of culture, technology, and politics that could occur in 50-200 years. It's easier if you are starting say, back in colonial America. But what if you are starting at modern day? How should I describe the setting of the year 2060, 2100, or 2200?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:53:10-07:00","id":612759,"title":"","content":"BP don't grow up only with time but also with experience. It's not the same things. Even been embraced from a particular powerful vampire let the new vampire to have a BP value higer than one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T17:12:38-07:00","id":612795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, and probably the most simple, is a lot of time skips. Is it acceptable to say. &quot;Okay, ten years pass. What did your character do to pass the time?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's easier if you are starting say, back in colonial America. But what if you are starting at modern day? How should I describe the setting of the year 2060, 2100, or 2200? </div> </div> </div>Do what you were suggesting. Start earlier. If you add in the future you're going to make that the focus of the game rather than your characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T15:01:22-07:00","id":614087,"title":"","content":"1- BP can be raised with XP. You don't have to do time skips for it to grow. You don't have to do time skips at all if you don't want to.<br /> <br /> 2- Everything else is at your discretion. Of course you can do time skips that way, no prob at all. But the future is however you want it to be. You don't have to make the future take the spotlight of your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T17:40:47-07:00","id":614323,"title":"","content":"I'm doing my Requiem game set in 2199. The Commonwealth of Carthage(slightly modified from the Danse Macabre version) has been steadily gaining control over the worlds power structures, with an eye toward &quot;coming out&quot;. They(the ominous, shadowy They) believe that they have a solid grip on the world now, and plan to reveal to the world the benevolent hand of the vampires on New Years Eve. The PCs are all vampires of middling age, between BP 2 to 4. None of them think it's a good idea. None of the NPC's, individually, has much confidence in the idea either. And yet, the ball is still rolling. It's too big to stop now, or so it seemed at the beginning.<br /> <br /> Being in the Future got my players very excited, as they all latched on to some personal vision of &quot;the Future&quot;, and used that to flesh out a very cool setting. With every new advance of technology that they gave me, they became more invested in the setting, and would provide examples of how the vampires use that new tech to further their own ends.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 08-03-2015, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T21:06:15-07:00","id":614502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612725-welcome-to-the-world-of-tomorrow?p=612759#post612759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BP don't grow up only with time but also with experience. It's not the same things. Even been embraced from a particular powerful vampire let the new vampire to have a BP value higer than one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the mod that uses blood beats/experience to up BP.<br /> Sort like a vamp version of arcane experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T01:12:11-07:00","id":614711,"title":"","content":"For a Mage game set in 2079 NYC, I have used this website : <a href=\"http://www.futuretimeline.net/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.futuretimeline.net/</a><br /> Maybe it'll give some idea for technologies, evolutions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/703-13th-hour","name":"13th Hour","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar703_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T02:56:15-07:00","id":614744,"title":"","content":"Also glossing over stuff like future tech is a decent way of modelling your players getting old and behind the times somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T03:02:16-07:00","id":614759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612725-welcome-to-the-world-of-tomorrow?p=614323#post614323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being in the Future got my players very excited, as they all latched on to some personal vision of &quot;the Future&quot;, and used that to flesh out a very cool setting. With every new advance of technology that they gave me, they became more invested in the setting, and would provide examples of how the vampires use that new tech to further their own ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solid STing there. Sounds like a good story too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T16:08:11-07:00","id":615683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612725-welcome-to-the-world-of-tomorrow#post612725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, and more difficult for me, is the changes of culture, technology, and politics that could occur in 50-200 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. It's always been a giant pain in the ass for me to reconcile &quot;serenely drifting through the ages, gradually becoming a godlike monstrosity&quot; with &quot;it's taken you twenty more-or-less indistinguishable years but now you run the city because you're 20th level, and oh crap you've really <i>really</i> advanced fast compared to the average model, haven't you? <i>Damn</i>...&quot;.<br /> <br /> It becomes a brawl between concentrating on historical settings (which take more research and force you to swap out mortal contacts periodically) and concentrating on what you're doing in just the one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T19:04:07-07:00","id":615900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612725-welcome-to-the-world-of-tomorrow#post612725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one thing that I have difficulty with is the duration of time that can pass in world in a campaign for vampire. In most games years, or decades at most will pass. But for vampire, to get the players to blood potency 3 or 4 without diablere would take some time. This brings up two problems for me.<br /> <br /> First, and probably the most simple, is a lot of time skips. Is it acceptable to say. &quot;Okay, ten years pass. What did your character do to pass the time?&quot;<br /> <br /> Secondly, and more difficult for me, is the changes of culture, technology, and politics that could occur in 50-200 years. It's easier if you are starting say, back in colonial America. But what if you are starting at modern day? How should I describe the setting of the year 2060, 2100, or 2200?</div> </div> </div> </div>Orions arm has a very good SF setting for far future. They have mapped out about 8,000 years.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.orionsarm.com/xcms.php?r=oa-intro\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.orionsarm.com/images/oa_2018/logo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.orionsarm.com/xcms.php?r=oa-intro\" target=\"_blank\"> Welcome to the Orion's Arm Universe Project </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.orionsarm.com/xcms.php?r=oa-intro\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.orionsarm.com/xcms.php?r=oa-intro </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Orion's Arm, orions arm, OA, worldbuilding, shared world, science fiction, sci fi, sci-fi, scifi, sf, hard science, hard science fiction, hard sf, future history, augmentations, mods </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:22:14-07:00","id":616046,"title":"","content":"You could use events to freeze civilization and technology.<br /> 2020 - Iran nukes Israel<br /> 2021 - Arabs begin testing nukes to create the Persian/Arab Cold War<br /> 2025 - Sunni (or Shia) Radicals acquire nukes from the Persians or Arabs, or scavenge from the remnants of Israel to attack anybody in the region resulting in retaliation against the Persian and Arab nations plus a bit of Europe and Russia for good measure which causes Europe and Russia to retaliate and China to preemptively strike creating a nuclear winter from the East versus West attacking each other because they can't exactly know where the missiles are actually going, basically WW3<br /> 2050 - Climate recovers but civilizations have fallen apart so the average technology level is circa 1950<br /> 2060 - Cultural revival and civilizations have reformed with an almost full recovery of technology<br /> <br /> Don't think people are reasonable? More massive nuclear war resulting in the climate recovery not occuring until 2100. Decades of living with a focus on survival over civilized behaviors has resulted in tribes of savage people preying on the last remnants of old civilizations. Civilizations at current cultural and technological levels don't recover for a 100 years.<br /> <br /> Or go the Sci-Fi route. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:03:25-07:00","id":616321,"title":"","content":"The world of darkness isn't our world 1 for 1. Why not tell a tale of technological stagnation? There are all sort of horrors out there, they could easily have an effect on the world's development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T16:59:40-07:00","id":618222,"title":"","content":"You could even use the God-Machine or other inscrutable power to explain out this stagnation, giving both a background explanation and a big mystery for your PCs if they want to explore this further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T07:54:35-07:00","id":619996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612725-welcome-to-the-world-of-tomorrow?p=616046#post616046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could use events to freeze civilization and technology.<br /> 2020 - Iran nukes Israel<br /> 2021 - Arabs begin testing nukes to create the Persian/Arab Cold War<br /> 2025 - Sunni (or Shia) Radicals acquire nukes from the Persians or Arabs, or scavenge from the remnants of Israel to attack anybody in the region resulting in retaliation against the Persian and Arab nations plus a bit of Europe and Russia for good measure which causes Europe and Russia to retaliate and China to preemptively strike creating a nuclear winter from the East versus West attacking each other because they can't exactly know where the missiles are actually going, basically WW3<br /> 2050 - Climate recovers but civilizations have fallen apart so the average technology level is circa 1950<br /> 2060 - Cultural revival and civilizations have reformed with an almost full recovery of technology<br /> <br /> Don't think people are reasonable? More massive nuclear war resulting in the climate recovery not occuring until 2100. Decades of living with a focus on survival over civilized behaviors has resulted in tribes of savage people preying on the last remnants of old civilizations. Civilizations at current cultural and technological levels don't recover for a 100 years.<br /> <br /> Or go the Sci-Fi route. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did have an idea for switching the setting into more of a post-apocalyptic setting. I'm trying to think of how to make it so the players would have a hand in the world's downfall. One of my NPCs claims to have the ark of the covenant. But he's also insane. So it may be the Ark, or it may be a nuke that slipped through the cracks after the cold war. Regardless he has a dangerous item that could trigger the nations to each retaliate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T08:56:45-07:00","id":620097,"title":"","content":"Or it could be the Ark which could be used to call a meteor down from the heavens to create a change in climate, less deadly radiation floating around that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T10:40:12-07:00","id":620256,"title":"","content":"For Future Tech, the assumption I told my players to assume was that outside of special call-outs*, assume that the biggest technological difference is density, availability, and quality. The city is built on top of the old city, which was in turn built on top of the city before that. Public transportation is denser than ever. The internet was so good that they put it in people's brains as implantable hardware. Crypto-currencies! Super-hackers! All of the Conservative fears for the future have come true! All of the Liberal fears for the future have come true! An insidious distopia that any reasonable person would fight to defend, because if you don't spend too long thinking about it it seems like heaven.<br /> <br /> Basically, I tried to imagine how a conspiracy of monsters would solve all of today's problems. If there is new sci-fi tech, it's because I let my players invent it.<br /> <br /> *Plasma weapons, the Tact-Ax(combination baton/taser/staff/fire ax/snare that is the favored sidearm of the Police), C.A.S.I.E. Implantable Nueral Net(The internet in your brain! My players wanted a little Ghost in the Shell), Low-rent Holodecks.. ALL of these are things that were supplied by my players, who continue to refine their capabilities and limits, and how they shape the World of Tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 08-08-2015, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:49:45-07:00","id":620660,"title":"","content":"I would look into cyberpunk ideas; recommending deus ex human revolution. the original is good, but I recommend HR because it shows that the future has different trends and clothes then the present; still regonizable as modern but that you can see changes. where as a lot of future stuff typically imagines average clothing looking similar to current. Not to mention the various different tech will give people ideas with what to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}